# Korenix JetI/O 6510.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Korenix JetI/O 6510 Industrial Intelligent Ethernet I/O Server
# | 
# | Source: JetI/O 6510 User's Manual V0.1 (Jan. 2008)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (Ethernet port 502); FC03 read holding, FC04 read input, FC06 write single
# | Module: 8-channel analog input, 16-bit, configurable range per-module (not per-channel):
# | 08H=±10V, 09H=±5V, 0AH=±1V, 0BH=±500mV, 0CH=±150mV, 0DH=±20mA
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Measured analog values live in the FC04 Input Register space (Modicon 30001-30008),
# | addresses 0-7. Holding registers (FC03, Modicon 40001-40041) are configuration only.
# | Input register values are signed 16-bit; units depend on selected range
# | (e.g. ±10V range: -10000 ~ +10000 = mV; ±20mA range: -20000 ~ +20000 = µA).
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Korenix
@model=JetI/O 6510
@description=8-CH analog input Ethernet I/O server, Modbus/TCP. Range set globally at holding reg 10 (08=±10V,09=±5V,0A=±1V,0B=±500mV,0C=±150mV,0D=±20mA). Measured values in FC04 input registers addr 0-7 (s16, mV or µA). Holding regs: watchdog (0-2), firmware/name (3-4), calibration (6-12), per-channel low/high alarm thresholds ch0-7 (13-28), channel mask (29), alarm enable (30), SNMP trap config (31-40).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/korenix-jetio-6510.toml; Source: JetI/O 6510 User's Manual V0.1 (Jan. 2008). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

